## Q5: Old Frontend Folder - Why Keep It? 🗑️ CAN DELETE

### What It Is
```
frontend/
├── app.py              # Streamlit app (183 lines)
└── requirements.txt    # streamlit, requests
```

**Purpose:** Quick Streamlit prototype/demo for testing backend APIs.

**Current State:**
- ❌ Not deployed to production
- ❌ Not used by Vercel
- ⚠️ Still referenced in [docker-compose.yml](file:///Users/onronder/axial/docker-compose.yml)
- ❌ Not maintained (last commits from early development)

### Production Uses
- ✅ Vercel → deploys [frontend-new/](file:///Users/onronder/axial/frontend-new) only
- ✅ Railway backend → no frontend
- ❌ Docker compose → references old frontend (but not used)

### Recommendation: DELETE

**Safe to delete:**
1. Remove [frontend/](file:///Users/onronder/axial/frontend) folder
2. Remove `frontend:` service from [docker-compose.yml](file:///Users/onronder/axial/docker-compose.yml)
3. Keep [frontend-new/](file:///Users/onronder/axial/frontend-new) (production)

**If you want to keep for local testing:**
- Rename to `frontend-legacy/` or `frontend-demo/`
- Update docker-compose.yml references
- Add to .gitignore

